# web-knowledge configuration reference.
#
# The real file is data/config.env. `npm run setup` (or ./install.sh) writes
# it for you — you only need this file if you prefer to write it by hand:
#   mkdir -p data && cp config.example.env data/config.env && chmod 600 data/config.env
# then fill in values and (re)start: docker compose up -d
#
# Any key left empty disables that provider; the cascade moves on to the next.

# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude, used to rewrite queries and synthesize answers (/search only).
# https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Callers send this as the X-WK-Token header on /search and /read.
# Any long random string, e.g. the output of:  openssl rand -hex 32
WK_API_TOKEN=

# ── SEARCH PROVIDERS (tried in this order) ──────────
# Tavily — search + page content in one call. https://tavily.com/
TAVILY_API_KEY=
# SearXNG — self-hosted, runs automatically alongside, no key.
# Exa — https://exa.ai/
EXA_API_KEY=
# Brave Search — https://brave.com/search/api/
BRAVE_API_KEY=
# Serper.dev (Google results) — https://serper.dev/
SERPER_API_KEY=
# DuckDuckGo — no key, always last.

# ── PAGE READING PROVIDERS (tried in this order) ────
# Raw HTTP, then Jina Reader — no keys.
# Tavily Extract reuses TAVILY_API_KEY above.
# Firecrawl — https://firecrawl.dev/
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# ── CACHE ───────────────────────────────────────────
# How long a cached answer stays fresh; each cache hit extends it again.
CACHE_TTL_HOURS=24
